  "configuration_id": "config_001",
  "reason": "With no prior evidence, the most informative first experiment is the simplest possible baseline: RNA-only, single profile, PCA (n=2000). This establishes a performance floor and a reference point against which all other design choices (richer encoders, multiprofile aggregation, image modality, fusion) can be judged. If this minimal configuration already performs competitively, it challenges the assumption that complex encoders or multimodality are necessary, saving budget. If it underperforms, it identifies which dimension (representation, profile, modality) to explore next. Choosing the most parsimonious configuration first avoids conflating the effects of multiple design changes and gives the clearest signal for subsequent experiments."
}

